The `generateName` method first generates a prefix based on the first three characters of the star's location, converted to uppercase. It then generates a suffix based on the star's brightness and distance, using a combination of a "B" or "D" character for brightness (depending on whether the brightness is greater than 5), and an "A", "B", or "C" character for distance (depending on whether the distance is less than 10, less than 100, or greater than or equal to 100).
The method then combines the prefix and suffix to form a candidate name, and recursively generates new names until a distinct name is found (i.e., one that is not already in the set of existing names). Once a distinct name is found, it is added to the set of existing names and returned.
