From an ethical standpoint, blockchain raises concerns around privacy and data protection, as well as the potential for the technology to be used for illegal activities such as money laundering and terrorism financing. Additionally, the legal implications of blockchain are still being explored, with questions around liability and jurisdiction yet to be fully addressed.
