```
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;
public class FrequencyAnalyzer {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String text = "This is a sample text for frequency analysis.";
        Map<Character, Integer> letterFrequencyTable = generateLetterFrequencyTable(text);
        Map<String, Integer> digraphFrequencyTable = generateNgramFrequencyTable(text, 2);
        Map<String, Integer> trigraphFrequencyTable = generateNgramFrequencyTable(text, 3);
        System.out.println("Letter frequency table: " + letterFrequencyTable);
        System.out.println("Digraph frequency table: " + digraphFrequencyTable);
        System.out.println("Trigraph frequency table: " + trigraphFrequencyTable);
    }
    private static Map<Character, Integer> generateLetterFrequencyTable(String text) {
        Map<Character, Integer> frequencyTable = new HashMap<>();
        for (char c : text.toCharArray()) {
            if (Character.isLetter(c)) {
                frequencyTable.put(c, frequencyTable.getOrDefault(c, 0) + 1);
            }
        }
        return frequencyTable;
    }
    private static Map<String, Integer> generateNgramFrequencyTable(String text, int n) {
        Map<String, Integer> frequencyTable = new HashMap<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < text.length() - n + 1; i++) {
            String ngram = text.substring(i, i + n);
            if (ngram.matches("[a-zA-Z]+")) {
                frequencyTable.put(ngram, frequencyTable.getOrDefault(ngram, 0) + 1);
            }
        }
        return frequencyTable;
    }
}
```
In this code, we have two helper methods `generateLetterFrequencyTable` and `generateNgramFrequencyTable` that generate frequency tables for letters and n-grams, respectively. The `generateLetterFrequencyTable` method loops through each character in the text and counts the frequency of each letter. The `generateNgramFrequencyTable` method loops through each n-gram in the text (where n is either 2 or 3) and counts the frequency of each n-gram.
To use this code, simply replace the `text` variable with your own text and run the `main` method. The output will be the frequency tables for letters, digraphs, and trigraphs in the text.

